Title: Paper Boats
Author: Rough Cut release run

EXT. HARBOUR WALL - DAWN

Grey water slaps the stones. ELENA, a young woman with ink-stained fingers, folds a paper boat from a letter.

ELENA
One more.

EXT. HARBOUR STEPS - DAWN

She sets the boat on the water. It spins, then drifts toward the open sea.

INT. BAKERY - MORNING

Warm light. MARCO, an old man dusted with flour, slides a tray of bread from the oven.

MARCO
You're up early.

ELENA
I couldn't sleep.

INT. BAKERY - CONTINUOUS

Marco pours two coffees and pushes one across the counter.

MARCO
Another letter?

ELENA
The last one.

EXT. FISHING PIER - DAY

Nets dry in the sun. A fisherman, TOMAS, a middle-aged man in a blue cap, lifts a soaked paper boat from his net.

TOMAS
Now what is this?

EXT. FISHING PIER - CONTINUOUS

He unfolds it carefully. Faded handwriting runs across the page.

TOMAS
For whoever finds this.

EXT. VILLAGE SQUARE - AFTERNOON

Tomas crosses the square, the damp letter in his hand, and stops at the bakery door.

INT. BAKERY - AFTERNOON

The bell rings. Elena looks up from the counter.

TOMAS
Is this yours?

ELENA
It was.

EXT. HARBOUR WALL - SUNSET

Elena and Tomas sit side by side. She folds a new boat; he watches.

TOMAS
Where does it go?

ELENA
Wherever it's needed.

EXT. HARBOUR STEPS - DUSK

Two paper boats drift out together on the golden water.
